            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "well_echo": {
            "id": "well_echo",
            "text": "[The names stop.]\n[That has not happened in four hundred years. Somewhere in Dusthaven a woman is holding four crystals to a frequency and weeping, and here, in a hole in the floor, a shape stands up out of the dark and is a woman, roughly, and is thirty-one, roughly, and is looking at your chest.]\n— Oh. Oh, they sent another one. —\n— Listen. I have very little of this. Listen. It is not seven doors, at the bottom. It is four, and every one of them is an ending, and they will tell you that is generous. —\n— I could not do it. I stood there nine years' worth of tired and I could not pick an ending, so I picked the one that was work instead, because work is not an ending, work is a tomorrow. —\n— It has been twenty-two years of tomorrow. —\n[The shape puts out a hand toward you and cannot reach, because a hole in a floor is not a person.]\n— Do not come and rescue me. Come and RELIEVE me. Those are different and the difference is the whole of it. —\n[The names start again. Hers is not in them. It never was.]",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "[Step back.]",
                "nextNodeId": "echo_end",
                "conditions": []
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "echo_end": {
            "id": "echo_end",
            "text": "[The Well reads its list. Somewhere south of here, a woman has been standing a post for twenty-two years.]",
