            ]
          },
          "well_offer": {
            "id": "well_offer",
            "text": "[The names stop, briefly, which is the Well's entire vocabulary for surprise.]\n— Relief. —\n— I was guarded. When people still came to be named, four of the Archive's knights stood at the rim, and they were relieved at the turn of every watch, and that was the arrangement and it was a good arrangement. —\n— The last relief did not come. It has not come for four hundred years. They are still standing. There is nothing in them now but the standing. —\n— I cannot dismiss them. I am a hole in a floor. I read a list. —\n— Go out to the rifts and relieve my guard. —",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_QUEST",
                "target": "the_well_of_names",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
